== 4.7 Chapter 4 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The novel's central concern is],
  [the pressure to migrate and the cost of staying],
  [the history of Lagos],
  [the running of a football team],
  [the politics of a university]
)

#mcq(2, [A theme, as the paper uses the word, is],
  [the setting of the novel],
  [the name of a chapter],
  [a claim the novel makes and supports],
  [a subject the novel mentions]
)

#mcq(3, [The visit to Badagry is significant chiefly because it],
  [gives the pupils a holiday],
  [draws a parallel between the slave trade and modern migration],
  [shows Bepo's skill as an organiser],
  [introduces the Akran of Badagry]
)

#mcq(4, [The main setting of the novel is],
  [London],
  [Ibadan],
  [Lekki, Lagos],
  [Abuja]
)

#mcq(5, [Which of the following is mentioned in the novel but never shown?],
  [Ibadan],
  [Badagry],
  [Lekki],
  [London]
)

#mcq(6, [The novel's treatment of migration suggests that],
  [migration is always an improvement],
  [migration can be reasonable and still be a loss],
  [migration is irrelevant to the story],
  [migration is always a mistake]
)

#mcq(7, [The figures Seri's salary and Bepo's UK post are given in order to],
  [criticise the British economy],
  [show that Bepo cannot do arithmetic],
  [make the material case for leaving],
  [prove that nursing pays better than teaching]
)

#mcq(8, [Beesway Group of Schools stands in the novel for],
  [the school Bepo founded],
  [a school whose owner cannot be corrected],
  [the school Seri attended],
  [the best school in Lagos]
)

#mcq(9, [Fruitful Future, the school Bepo co-founded, stands for],
  [the model school of the novel],
  [an honest attempt that failed on economics],
  [the corruption of private education],
  [a school owned by the board]
)

#mcq(10, [The discovery of the cooperative society chiefly illustrates],
  [the dishonesty of teachers],
  [Bepo's incompetence with money],
  [the board's fear of a financially independent staff],
  [the failure of academic standards]
)

#mcq(11, [Mr Ogo's offer of a rite at Fruitful Future represents],
  [a legitimate business proposal],
  [a religious duty],
  [the wish for success without work],
  [a test of Bepo's courage]
)

#mcq(12, [The excursion programme in Chapter 9 exists chiefly to],
  [teach the pupils the country they belong to],
  [improve the school's results],
  [prepare the pupils for study abroad],
  [raise money for the school]
)

#mcq(13, [When the pupils laugh at Mushin, Ajegunle and Ijora, Bepo tells them that],
  [those places should be avoided],
  [being born in such a place condemns nobody to poverty],
  [the school should build there],
  [the poor are happier than the rich]
)

#mcq(14, [The novel's attitude to Nigerian education is best described as],
  [indifferent],
  [uncritically admiring],
  [critical but hopeful],
  [entirely despairing]
)

#mcq(15, [The contrast between Beesway and Stardom suggests that a school's integrity depends on],
  [the size of its fees],
  [the number of its pupils],
  [whether its owner can be corrected],
  [the quality of its buildings]
)

#mcq(16, [What the board fears about the staff is that they might],
  [steal the school's money],
  [refuse to teach],
  [leave and establish a rival school],
  [report the school to the ministry]
)

#mcq(17, [The novel treats ritual and superstition as],
  [a temptation to succeed without work],
  [an authentic cultural practice],
  [the religion of the poor],
  [a harmless eccentricity]
)

#mcq(18, [Mrs Ignatius's story chiefly illustrates],
  [the dangers of DNA testing],
  [the emotional and family cost of migration],
  [the dishonesty of parents],
  [the weakness of the school's records]
)

#mcq(19, [The prefect election in Chapter 8 illustrates],
  [the pupils' indifference to office],
  [the fairness of school democracy],
  [Bepo's love of ceremony],
  [how closely school politics mirrors adult society]
)

#mcq(20, [Bepo's refusal of the rite at Fruitful Future illustrates],
  [his dislike of parents],
  [that rituals do not work],
  [that integrity has a price],
  [his fear of the occult]
)

#mcq(21, [The setting that carries the state as an obstacle course is],
  [the passport office in Ibadan],
  [the staff quarters at Beesway],
  [the assembly ground at Stardom],
